{
  "//": [
    "TEMPLATE, NOT SERVED. This file is deliberately not routed by vercel.json,",
    "because publishing an apple-app-site-association whose appID is a",
    "placeholder is worse than publishing none: Apple's CDN caches the file, and",
    "a cached invalid one makes universal links fail in a way that takes days to",
    "clear. It is completed and routed in one step, once a real Apple Team ID",
    "exists.",
    "",
    "TO ACTIVATE, three edits and nothing else:",
    "  1. replace APPLE_TEAM_ID below with the real 10-character Team ID from",
    "     developer.apple.com > Membership. Do not guess it; it is not derivable",
    "     from anything in this repository.",
    "  2. rename this file to apple-app-site-association.json",
    "  3. add ONE route to vercel.json, immediately beside the assetlinks route",
    "     that is already there, and before { \"handle\": \"filesystem\" }:",
    "",
    "       { \"src\": \"/\\\\.well-known/apple-app-site-association\", \"dest\": \"/apple-app-site-association.json\" }",
    "",
    "     Routing to a .json file is what makes Vercel serve it as",
    "     application/json, which Apple requires and which a file with no",
    "     extension would not get. It adds no Serverless Function, so the 12/12",
    "     budget is unaffected.",
    "  4. rename ios/App/App/App.entitlements.template to App.entitlements and",
    "     add it to the App target in Xcode.",
    "",
    "The path Apple fetches is https://<host>/.well-known/apple-app-site-association",
    "with no extension and no redirect. Apple does not follow redirects for this",
    "file.",
    "",
    "PATHS: /auth and everything under it, matching the Android App Link",
    "intent-filter's android:pathPrefix=\"/auth\" exactly. Nothing else is claimed",
    "-- claiming / would hand every link to the site to the app, including the",
    "account shell and the legal pages, which must stay in the browser.",
    "",
    "This key is ignored by Apple; JSON has no comments and a \"//\" member is the",
    "conventional way to leave one in a file that must stay valid JSON."
  ],
  "applinks": {
    "details": [
      {
        "appIDs": ["APPLE_TEAM_ID.com.velvetviking.valhalla"],
        "components": [
          { "/": "/auth", "comment": "the magic-link landing itself" },
          { "/": "/auth/*", "comment": "and anything beneath it" }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "webcredentials": {
    "apps": ["APPLE_TEAM_ID.com.velvetviking.valhalla"]
  }
}
